{"toolCallId":"call_66b158bd93c64ab781fbb540d8a03c3a","title":"Wrote ./specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path)\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n<!-- FILL: Keep the prefix table and add the two shell variables this task list uses. GOOD: `S` is the script path. `P` is the packet path. WEAK: Variables are defined below. -->\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n<!-- FILL: Replace the sample tasks with the real setup steps. Each task names a file and a verify command. GOOD: T001 Read the output block in `recommend-level.sh`. Verify: `rg -n 'Recommended Level'` prints one line. WEAK: T001 Set up the project. -->\n\n- [ ] T001 Create project structure\n- [ ] T002 Install dependencies\n- [ ] T003 [P] Configure development tools\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n<!-- FILL: Write one implementation task per file change. Add a `Verify:` line with the command and its expected output. GOOD: T002 Add the `--quiet` branch. Verify: `--quiet` prints one line. WEAK: T002 Implement the feature. -->\n\n- [ ] T004 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 1]\n- [ ] T005 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 2]\n- [ ] T006 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 3]\n- [ ] T007 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Add error handling]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n<!-- FILL: Write one verification task per requirement. Each one runs a command. GOOD: T003 Run both invocations. Verify: `wc -l` prints 1 and 17. WEAK: T003 Test everything. -->\n\n- [ ] T008 Test happy path manually\n- [ ] T009 Test edge cases\n- [ ] T010 Update documentation\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n<!-- FILL: Keep the three completion lines and add the one artifact that proves the phase is done. GOOD: `--quiet` prints one line and the suite passes. WEAK: Work is complete. -->\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n<!-- FILL: Name the spec and plan files. Add the decision record when the packet has one. GOOD: Specification: `spec.md`. Plan: `plan.md`. WEAK: See the other docs. -->\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path)\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\nTwo shell variables keep the commands short. Set them once before running any task:\n\n```bash\nS=.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh\nP=specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent\n```\n\n`S` is the script under change and `P` is this packet folder. `X` below stands for the `Overall Completion` percentage the baseline report prints.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Capture the current text report and its exit status (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" \"$P\" > /tmp/before.txt 2>/tmp/before.err; echo $?` prints `0`.\n- [ ] T002 Capture the current JSON report (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --json \"$P\" > /tmp/before.json; echo $?` prints `0`.\n- [ ] T003 Read the argument loop and the trailing exit path (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n 'exit 0' \"$S\"` prints the final `exit 0` that closes the main block.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T004 Add the `--min-percent <N>` case to the argument loop with integer range validation, storing the value in a new global (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent abc \"$P\"; echo $?` prints one `ERROR:` line and `1`.\n- [ ] T005 Replace the trailing `exit 0` with an explicit `if` gate that exits 3 when the reported completion is below `N` (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 100 \"$P\" >/dev/null; echo $?` prints `3` while the report is below 100, and `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 0 \"$P\" >/dev/null; echo $?` prints `0`.\n- [ ] T006 Add the option to the `show_help` text (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --help | rg -c 'min-percent'` prints `1`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T007 Diff the text report with and without the flag (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 0 \"$P\" > /tmp/after.txt; diff /tmp/before.txt /tmp/after.txt` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T008 Diff the JSON report with and without the flag (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --json --min-percent 0 \"$P\" > /tmp/after.json; diff /tmp/before.json /tmp/after.json` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T009 Check the below-threshold exit code (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent $((X + 1)) \"$P\" >/dev/null; echo $?` prints `3`.\n- [ ] T010 Check the boundary and above-threshold exit codes (`$S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent \"$X\" \"$P\" >/dev/null; echo $?` prints `0`, and the same with `$((X > 0 ? X - 1 : 0))` prints `0`.\n- [ ] T011 Check the runs that do not use the flag (`$S`). Verify: the plain, `--json`, `--verbose` and `--file` invocations each print `0` from `echo $?`.\n- [ ] T012 Run the strict validator on this packet (`$P`). Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh \"$P\" --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] The report diff is empty in text and JSON mode, and `--min-percent` exits 3 below the threshold and 0 at or above it\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":22,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":19}}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"write"}}
